<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19296" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gannītus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		gannio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a yelping</i> or <i>barking of
			dogs.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
				1070</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of sparrows, <i>a chirping</i>, <i>twittering</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p.
			175</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Of persons, <i>a snarling</i>, <i>grumbling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gannitibus lacessere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 5, 60, 21</span></i>
			; <i>a chattering</i>, <i>tattling</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 185</span></i>; <i>a whining</i>, <i>moaning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tristis Nerēidis morientis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 9,
					5, 4, § 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>